Game is "okay" right now, but not that great, as reviewers say since,I have no idea which version of game they played.
*Units shoot through walls, through some heavy obstacles, which didn't even explode or anything, we can just see that something did go through i;
*Action phase/movement delay. Need to wait like 10sec, before I can take my next action between units.Feels really, really annoying;
*FPS issues. All cut-scenes are total lagging festival for me. Turned off AA and AO, gameplay feels smothered now, but cut-scenes remain at the same condition;
*Character movement seems too accelerated after playing first XCOM? I'm not sure, that's just the way I felt first, when playing?
Will update more, when I'll have more time to test it out. Right now, I'll keep it as not recommended, till the developers take action against these problems. Although, gameplay is great and enjoyable, but these problems really are not cool and are pretty annoying.
EDIT:
*Camera - There seems to be a problems with camera. My unit was inside of building and I couldn't change floor,where my unit was located. Update: Yup,not only buildings...somehow I'm seeing black screen,when enemy is comming...no idea,where camera is aiming at.
